    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d21">

                <pb facs="0065" n="19" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v02/pg19"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72/5163½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of the British Special Mission</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Balfour</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-05-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">18 May, 1917</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: On that delightful
                    Sunday which we spent in the country I promised to send you the main points of a
                    statement which I made on foreign policy to the Imperial War Council. The
                    proceedings of the Imperial War Council are of course absolutely secret. I feel
                    that many of the problems dealt with are inadequately treated, but I trust that
                    you may find it of some value.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Arthur James Balfour</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d21-a1.xml" xpointer="d21-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
